!
! Period-averaged (SVEA) 3D example.  Seeded, helical undulator, diffraction
! on, beam matched to the undulator's natural focusing, no lattice.
!
! See inputs/simple/1D/averaged/averaged.in for what qAveraged and
! lambdarPerCell do and what the mode refuses at setup; this header covers only
! what is different in 3D.  The ordinary options are annotated in any other
! example in inputs/simple/, and in the user manual in $PUFFIN/doc/.
!
!--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------!
!                      3D IN AVERAGED MODE
!--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------!
!
! Only the z2 mesh is averaged.  x and y are unchanged - iNumNodesX/Y,
! sFModelLengthX/Y, iRedNodesX/Y and the diffraction step all mean exactly what
! they mean unaveraged, and diffraction still runs every sDiffFrac of a period.
! lambdarPerCell coarsens z2 and nothing else.
!
! sBeta = 0.0, deliberately.  THIS IS THE ONE THAT WILL CATCH YOU.  The z2
! absorbing boundary is sized in NODES, not in z2 - NBZ2_G = 37
! (puffin/lib/setup/setup_calcs.f90) - and an averaged z2 mesh has far fewer
! nodes for the same physical length.  dz2 = 4 pi rho lambdarPerCell, so this
! 20-unit model is 320 nodes here and the absorber is ~12% of it, where
! unaveraged at nodesPerLambdar = 12 the same length is 11x more nodes and the
! absorber is ~1%.  Coarsen further - lambdarPerCell = 4 gives 81 nodes - and
! the absorber is approaching half the mesh.  So leave sBeta at 0 as here, or
! check the node count first; it is the absolute count that matters, not the
! length.  See the W2 and W7 notes in
! AVERAGED_MODE_ROADMAP.md.
!
! qFocussing = .false. with a matched beam.  The undulator's natural focusing
! is always on - averaged mode period-averages it into cNatX/cNatY
! (getAvgFocusCoef) rather than dropping it - and qMatched_A = .true. in the
! beam file matches the beam to it, so the transverse envelope is constant.
! qFocussing adds a separate strong-focusing channel on top; it is off here so
! that any error in the averaged focusing shows up directly as a breathing
! beam rather than being masked.
!
! zundType = 'helical', so BOTH polarisation envelopes are in play: component 1
! is the x envelope, component 2 the y, each driven with its own coupling, and
! for a helical undulator they come out at B_y = i B_x.  The seed file sets
! sA0_X and sA0_Y together, the resonant helicity; any other seed polarisation
! is laid exactly too, but the opposite helicity does not couple to the beam.
! Averaged dumps carry both components, which is a layout change from
! unaveraged - see the nFieldComp dispatch in
! utilities/pyPlotting/plotPolarization.py.
!
!
!                      SIZE AND RANKS
!
! 41 x 41 x 320 nodes.  Puffin slab-decomposes z2 across ranks, so the z2 node
! count is what limits useful ranks; 319 is comfortable for the handful this
! deck needs.  It runs in 46 s on 2 ranks.  Coarsening z2 with
! lambdarPerCell is what makes an averaged run cheap, so watch that the mesh
! does not end up with fewer than a couple of nodes per rank - on a periodic
! mesh Puffin warns about that at setup, and that path is known to be broken.
!
! Ipk = 4000 in the beam file is well above a physical CLARA current, so that
! 120 periods reach clear exponential growth rather than seed-dominated
! lethargy.  It is a demonstration, not a machine.
!
!
! Begin input:-

&MDATA
 qOneD                  = .false.
 qFieldEvolve           = .true.
 qElectronsEvolve       = .true.
 qElectronFieldCoupling = .true.
 qFocussing             = .false.
 qDiffraction           = .true.
 qFilter                = .true.
 q_noise                = .false.
 qUndEnds               = .false.
 qAveraged              = .true.
 lambdarPerCell         = 1.0
 beam_file              = 'beam_file.in'
 sElectronThreshold     = 0.05
 iNumNodesX             = 41
 iNumNodesY             = 41
 nodesPerLambdar        = 12        ! ignored: qAveraged uses lambdarPerCell
 sFModelLengthX         = 8.0
 sFModelLengthY         = 8.0
 sFModelLengthZ2        = 20.0      ! the beam needs ~19; a shorter value is extended
 iRedNodesX             = 21
 iRedNodesY             = 21
 sFiltFrac              = 0.3
 sDiffFrac              = 1.0
 sBeta                  = 0.0       ! see the note above before changing
 seed_file              = 'seed_file.in'
 srho                   = 0.005
 sux                    = 1.0
 suy                    = 1.0
 saw                    = 1.0121809
 sgamma_r               = 456.40
 lambda_w               = 0.0275
 zundType               = 'helical'
 taper                  = 0.0
 lattFile               = ''
 stepsPerPeriod         = 2         ! 1 is converged too; 30 is usual unaveraged
 nPeriods               = 120
 sZ0                    = 0.0
 iWriteNthSteps         = 40
 iWriteIntNthSteps      = 2         ! one integrated write per undulator period
 /
